msgstr "**関連理論**: [検証済みアルゴリズム](../../explanation/validated_algorithms.md)"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:20002
#: c702e2913b7c4d63977a100e2fe4ccb6
msgid "1. Setup and Data Preparation"
msgstr "1\\. セットアップとデータの準備"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:20004
#: a805fef78b4f4a85858e442945bb600c
msgid "1.1 Imports and Parameters"
msgstr "1.1 インポートとパラメータ"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:50002
#: aca03bb8418a4161ab54200d11159ad2
msgid "1.2 Generate Colored Noise + Resonant Peak"
msgstr "1.2 カラードノイズ + 共振ピークの生成"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:50004
#: 3f1f0ddec27446e8af361a7ee9e6c47e
msgid "We create a time-series with:"
msgstr "以下の成分を含む時系列データを作成します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:50005
#: c5b71a7f510545eba51adf414f94dca5
msgid "**Background**: Pink noise (power-law ASD)"
msgstr "**バックグラウンド**: ピンクノイズ（べき乗則 ASD）"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:50006
#: e3616bd6520e48d4a4d9bc20df9976f2
msgid "**Signal**: Damped oscillation representing a resonant peak"
msgstr "**信号**: 共振ピークを表す減衰振動"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:80002
#: 5c0afe4cd41e4d0ba3866433c6e5378c
msgid "2. Spectrogram Construction"
msgstr "2\\. スペクトログラムの構築"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:80004
#: 749753883f2146b9b8767a1ae3ae736e
msgid "2.1 FFT Parameters"
msgstr "2.1 FFT パラメータ"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:80006
#: 0db0396eee994cdb93324472e08320ba
msgid ""
"We choose parameters to balance frequency resolution and statistical "
"reliability:"
msgstr "周波数分解能と統計的信頼性のバランスをとるパラメータを選択します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:80008
#: 321c3a94eb53417cb59c88af88c95fac
msgid "**fftlength**: Determines frequency resolution (df = 1/fftlength)"
msgstr "**fftlength**: 周波数分解能を決定（df = 1/fftlength）"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:80009
#: a322616f094b41ef9a989c8557bd8bf7
msgid "**stride**: Time step between spectrogram bins (typically = fftlength)"
msgstr "**stride**: スペクトログラムのビン間の時間ステップ（通常 = fftlength）"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:80010
#: 61e4ed69395f4c95b94ce8c5c8046e0b
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**overlap**: Overlap within each time-bin (for Welch averaging, 50% "
"recommended)"
msgstr "**overlap**: 各タイムビン内でのオーバーラップ（Welch 平均化に対して 50% 推奨）"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:80011
#: 33c9b2951a7c4d0180819d6d33a98661
msgid "**window**: Hann window minimizes spectral leakage"
msgstr "**window**: Hann 窓によりスペクトル漏洩を最小化"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:100002
#: 8a20372e3d03460fb3fc37faae846b8a
msgid "2.2 Generate Spectrogram"
msgstr "2.2 スペクトログラムの生成"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130002
#: 826be0e6892b4ea9b42cdf3c4207fcf0
msgid "3. Bootstrap PSD Estimation with Covariance Matrix"
msgstr "3\\. Bootstrap PSD 推定と共分散行列"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130004
#: 7d52d4c3118a4505989874b52a5f5dac
msgid "3.1 Why Bootstrap?"
msgstr "3.1 Bootstrap を使う理由"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130006
#: 81329cefb4354861abf871b998de1510
msgid ""
"Standard PSD estimation assumes frequency bins are **independent**, but this"
" breaks down when:"
msgstr "標準的な PSD 推定は周波数ビンが**独立**であることを仮定しますが、以下の場合にこの仮定は破れます。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130007
#: cc70427b05fe40f68058d013c7eb0523
#, python-format
msgid "Segments **overlap** (50% overlap introduces ~50% correlation)"
msgstr "セグメントが**オーバーラップ**している場合（50% オーバーラップで約 50% の相関が発生）"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130008
#: 1ea6af02a70a4ec7b522a9878b3f02f5
msgid "**Windowing** spreads spectral power across adjacent bins"
msgstr "**窓関数**がスペクトルパワーを隣接ビンに拡散させる場合"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130010
#: 3dd3d431aa0e46ab83ee164b386750d5
msgid "Bootstrap resampling captures these correlations by:"
msgstr "Bootstrap リサンプリングは以下の手順でこれらの相関を捕捉します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130011
#: 50e3d3449dfb42f9b183c0be4cac13f8
msgid "Resampling segments with replacement"
msgstr "セグメントを復元抽出でリサンプリング"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130012
#: 8b0d3bcfe5ca4c6b8033f0a4b7294a3a
msgid "Computing statistics for each resample"
msgstr "各リサンプルに対して統計量を計算"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130013
#: 890aba4a438e4d3cbf6516e5859c2266
msgid "Building the empirical covariance matrix"
msgstr "経験的共分散行列を構築"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:130015
#: 2bf70d8fe6344716b2542e483671206c
msgid "3.2 Bootstrap Parameters"
msgstr "3.2 Bootstrap パラメータ"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:150002
#: aaf0ff353c7944c5b37f33182c32c145
msgid "3.3 Run Bootstrap Estimation"
msgstr "3.3 Bootstrap 推定の実行"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:150004
#: f3359bbc7001470c8d06840f28646861
msgid "Using `return_map=True` returns both:"
msgstr "`return_map=True` を指定すると、以下の両方が返されます。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:150005
#: 935928a7a86e4429947786daeb38fd7a
msgid ""
"`psd_boot`: FrequencySeries with error bands (`error_low`, `error_high`)"
msgstr "`psd_boot`: 誤差バンド（`error_low`, `error_high`）付きの FrequencySeries"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:150006
#: 1f55d581044140148c7d915d4dee40da
msgid "`cov_map`: BifrequencyMap containing the full covariance matrix"
msgstr "`cov_map`: 完全な共分散行列を含む BifrequencyMap"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:170002
#: 895901c123f14adbafeebe982d5c678e
msgid "3.4 VIF (Variance Inflation Factor) Verification"
msgstr "3.4 VIF（分散膨張因子）の検証"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:170004
#: 3fd7917a3dbb4638a972c06159f9f899
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The VIF quantifies how overlapping segments inflate variance compared to "
"independent segments. For 50% overlap with Hann window, VIF ≈ 1.89 (Percival"
" & Walden 1993, Eq. 56)."
msgstr ""
"VIF は、独立セグメントと比較して、オーバーラップするセグメントが分散をどの程度膨張させるかを定量化します。 50% オーバーラップの Hann "
"窓に対して、VIF は約 1.89 です（Percival & Walden 1993, Eq. 56）。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:190002
#: 17900e734c4f48a1a8a3da91dcb45b73
msgid "3.5 Visualize Bootstrap Results"
msgstr "3.5 Bootstrap 結果の可視化"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:210002
#: a5be1557e6d64e7fb3f169430cb6bf12
msgid "**Key Observations:**"
msgstr "**主な観察結果:**"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:210003
#: 845af99c08d8466da18056cc25f220ee
msgid ""
"Adjacent frequency bins show **~0.25 correlation** from 50% time-segment "
"overlap"
msgstr "隣接する周波数ビンは、50% の時間セグメントオーバーラップにより**約 0.25 の相関**を示す"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:210004
#: f5f2604e6145439ca55899fa5e405d6d
msgid ""
"Correlation matrix shows **band-diagonal structure** (decay with distance)"
msgstr "相関行列は**帯状対角構造**（距離とともに減衰）を示す"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:210005
#: e5fe15462a9041599903fb21810167fc
msgid "With no rebinning, correlations between neighboring bins are preserved"
msgstr "リビニングなしでは、隣接ビン間の相関が保存される"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:210006
#: 96fb75fe46d54e5eb6d9aec95c0e61ce
msgid "Bootstrap captures this correlation in the covariance matrix"
msgstr "Bootstrap はこの相関を共分散行列に反映する"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:210007
#: a9faef6372d840e4894809fdb9357234
msgid "GLS fitting **utilizes** correlations; OLS **ignores** them"
msgstr "GLS フィッティングは相関を**活用**し、OLS は相関を**無視**する"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:220002
#: 068ac7868a8b4e4197164eeab5b36cad
msgid "4. Model Definition and GLS Fitting"
msgstr "4\\. モデル定義と GLS フィッティング"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:220004
#: 02873e4a0a2f4471921389ce2c3062e5
msgid "4.1 Define PSD Model"
msgstr "4.1 PSD モデルの定義"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:220006
#: fded53438020486480cf898e245516ee
msgid "We fit a model consisting of:"
msgstr "以下の成分からなるモデルをフィットします。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:220007
#: 8eb6fcffb4db4769aa7e5fd9ccfc768a
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Power-law background**: $A_{bg} (f/f_{ref})^{\\alpha}$"
msgstr "**べき乗則バックグラウンド**: $A_{bg} (f/f_{ref})^{\\alpha}$"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:220008
#: 9083116cbb6145a29fb0f6f974c97ac7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Lorentzian peak**: $A_{peak} \\frac{\\gamma^2}{(f-f_0)^2 + \\gamma^2}$ "
"where $\\gamma = f_0/(2Q)$"
msgstr ""
"**ローレンツ型ピーク**: $A_{peak} \\frac{\\gamma^2}{(f-f_0)^2 + \\gamma^2}$（ただし "
"$\\gamma = f_0/(2Q)$）"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:240002
#: d252b46a50064983b27cda58bf32ffec
msgid "4.2 Prepare Data for Fitting"
msgstr "4.2 フィッティング用データの準備"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:240004
#: 0c71b7da836943018a1a49a65e13cab4
msgid ""
"We crop the frequency range to focus on the region around the peak, and "
"prepare the corresponding covariance sub-matrix."
msgstr "ピーク周辺の周波数範囲にクロップし、対応する共分散部分行列を準備します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:260002
#: ed70d9a136884221b37f548513fc09bd
msgid "4.3 Initial Parameter Guesses and Bounds"
msgstr "4.3 初期パラメータの推定値と範囲"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:260004
#: 8fe1c91fd24145ebb5649d7881729dd4
msgid ""
"Good initial guesses help the optimizer converge to the correct minimum."
msgstr "適切な初期推定値を設定することで、最適化が正しい最小値に収束しやすくなります。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:260006
#: 931d3510f7e14f12b5584127af4ca915
msgid ""
"In this synthetic example, the center frequency is known to be near 100 Hz "
"and the resonance is a moderately broad commissioning line rather than an "
"arbitrarily narrow delta-like feature. Use bounds to encode that prior "
"knowledge so the optimizer does not explain broadband structure by pushing "
"`f0` or `Q` into nonphysical corners."
msgstr ""
"この合成例では中心周波数が 100 Hz 付近だと分かっており、対象は極端に鋭いデルタ線ではなく、ある程度幅を持つ commissioning line"
" です。その事前知識を bounds に入れて、`f0` や `Q` が不自然な端へ逃げることで広帯域構造を説明してしまうのを防ぎます。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:290002
#: b9d70dea0845472fb6e513f66a575a90
msgid "4.4 Run GLS Fitting"
msgstr "4.4 GLS フィッティングの実行"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:290004
#: 7260db0d3711468bb0bf2b45ead295d2
msgid ""
"By passing `cov=BifrequencyMap`, `fit_series` automatically uses "
"**Generalized Least Squares** which accounts for the full covariance "
"structure."
msgstr ""
"`cov=BifrequencyMap` を渡すことで、`fit_series` "
"は完全な共分散構造を考慮した**一般化最小二乗法（GLS）**を自動的に使用します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:290006
#: b38455d9915d476aac54aa16c532db40
msgid ""
"For the notebook-sized example here, GLS usually finishes in seconds, while "
"the MCMC step below is typically the longest part and often takes on the "
"order of minutes depending on walker count, step count, and hardware."
msgstr ""
"このノートブック規模の例では、GLS は通常数秒で終わります。一方、後半の MCMC は walker 数・step "
"数・計算機性能に応じて、分単位の実行時間になることがあります。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:310002
#: 31963f4b50f2420aa619c88a8606ba2e
msgid "4.5 Analyze Fit Results"
msgstr "4.5 フィッティング結果の解析"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:310004
#: f05b0e4e76854dd7b3f09d01cc1207c4
msgid ""
"For commissioning use, treat `f0` and `Q` as the primary diagnostics. The "
"absolute `A_peak` normalization is more sensitive to window leakage, "
"bootstrap median bias, and the PSD/ASD convention than the line center or "
"linewidth, so read it as an effective line-strength parameter rather than "
"the most robust truth-matching check."
msgstr ""
"commissioning で主要な診断量として重視すべきなのは `f0` と `Q` です。 絶対的な `A_peak` の規格化は、window "
"leakage、bootstrap median のバイアス、PSD/ASD 規約の影響を line center や linewidth "
"より強く受けます。そのため、ここでは厳密な真値一致よりも effective line-strength parameter として読みます。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:340002
#: a1c14b3577e144729bf6ad362fd87f96
msgid "5. MCMC Uncertainty Evaluation"
msgstr "5\\. MCMC による不確かさの評価"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:340004
#: 0bbaef37f9f44718bf02a3c7cd05b5c6
msgid ""
"MCMC (Markov Chain Monte Carlo) provides a more robust estimation of "
"parameter uncertainties and correlations. Treat it as the expensive "
"validation pass after the faster GLS estimate."
msgstr ""
"MCMC（マルコフ連鎖モンテカルロ法）は、パラメータの不確かさと相関のより頑健な推定を提供します。 まず GLS で初期評価を行い、MCMC "
"は計算コストの高い確認段階として使うのが実務的です。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:340007
#: 24be3c7874e04388b40cfe0e4e38865c
msgid "5.1 Run MCMC"
msgstr "5.1 MCMC の実行"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:360002
#: a7d9cb1a936d47cea1dcdda719463d8e
msgid "5.2 Convergence Diagnostics"
msgstr "5.2 収束診断"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:380002
#: 0ff2625db1b54d78be5cf3b84c8a0f44
msgid "5.3 Corner Plot and Trace Plots"
msgstr "5.3 コーナープロットとトレースプロット"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:410002
#: 3ed00661375f4efdb45cc09e2217c0df
msgid "6. GLS vs OLS Comparison"
msgstr "6\\. GLS と OLS の比較"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:410004
#: 9abb403103da414da9a831bc8c71eef0
msgid "6.1 Run OLS Fit (Diagonal Covariance Only)"
msgstr "6.1 OLS フィッティングの実行（対角共分散のみ）"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:410006
#: 696a19bec0de4b2282c5baa1402b60a1
msgid ""
"OLS (Ordinary Least Squares) ignores off-diagonal correlations, using only "
"the diagonal variances."
msgstr "OLS（通常最小二乗法）は非対角相関を無視し、対角分散のみを使用します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:430002
#: c1d813de6bf749de88c9a4cdefe192e2
msgid "6.2 Compare GLS and OLS Results"
msgstr "6.2 GLS と OLS の結果比較"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460002
#: cb678be055524fe8a43f1eb75cb1fc93
msgid "6.3 Key Insights"
msgstr "6.3 重要な知見"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460004
#: 1c5c5a672e3744dfb625258ba5b3bf25
msgid "**GLS errors are typically larger than OLS errors** because:"
msgstr "**GLS の誤差は一般的に OLS の誤差よりも大きくなります。** その理由は以下の通りです。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460006
#: 9411817860e64ad992e1549f5e752279
msgid ""
"**OLS underestimates uncertainties** by ignoring positive correlations "
"between adjacent bins"
msgstr "**OLS は不確かさを過小評価**する（隣接ビン間の正の相関を無視するため）"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460007
#: 976b903ac29e4c52af131d97690a3c44
msgid "**GLS properly accounts** for the reduced effective degrees of freedom"
msgstr "**GLS は有効自由度の減少を適切に考慮**する"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460008
#: dfe4d7f3ab504c65b3affc8ca95b58b4
msgid ""
"The error ratio (GLS/OLS > 1) reflects the **true impact of correlations**"
msgstr "誤差比（GLS/OLS > 1）は**相関の真の影響**を反映する"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460010
#: 2ed40d17c27f49a29048b370e688c540
msgid "**Expected with ~0.25 correlation**: GLS errors 10-30% larger than OLS"
msgstr "**約 0.25 の相関が存在する場合の期待値**: GLS 誤差は OLS より 10-30% 大きくなる"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460012
#: 88ad5dedb81c4fbead203daedc8f52ce
msgid "**Why GLS differs from OLS**:"
msgstr "**GLS が OLS と異なる理由**:"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460013
#: 4a5bdff5c5d34c94969bdb9a913288b6
msgid "OLS assumes independence → underestimates uncertainties"
msgstr "OLS は独立性を仮定 → 不確かさを過小評価"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460014
#: beadf6856aa84b7b8b7b5221d9ecf472
msgid "GLS accounts for correlation → reduces effective degrees of freedom"
msgstr "GLS は相関を考慮 → 有効自由度を削減"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460015
#: 54e7a53b1bf74be4a0ab7a00274708e6
msgid "Error ratio (GLS/OLS) quantifies correlation impact"
msgstr "誤差比（GLS/OLS）は相関の影響を定量化"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460016
#: c569588364ba4488847ffc3cb21ad7b5
#, python-format
msgid ""
"With 50% overlap: ~0.25 correlation leads to meaningful GLS vs OLS "
"differences"
msgstr "50% オーバーラップの場合: 約 0.25 の相関が GLS と OLS の間に有意な差をもたらす"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460018
#: 5b6c9c825c534b80845a7e48baa45a65
msgid "**Practical implications:**"
msgstr "**実用上の示唆:**"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460019
#: ba324fe2024c434c8892f3501da4b683
msgid "OLS may produce overconfident (too small) error bars"
msgstr "OLS は過信した（小さすぎる）誤差バーを生成する可能性がある"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460020
#: 4d0d513e15c748faa220ccc44316502e
msgid "GLS provides more honest uncertainty estimates"
msgstr "GLS はより正直な不確かさの推定を提供する"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:460021
#: c0975609714d4cc18547ac8df016586e
msgid "For precision measurements, GLS is essential"
msgstr "精密測定においては GLS が不可欠である"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470002
#: fdf5b8e51ed34b5598fc41ebae04b235
msgid "7. Summary and Best Practices"
msgstr "7\\. まとめとベストプラクティス"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470004
#: 4144f7400bd54112a8b3554e9ef992a8
msgid "Key Takeaways"
msgstr "主なポイント"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470006
#: 161e6d1f321e4faeb9c2c5cd40609d3f
msgid ""
"**Bootstrap PSD estimation** provides both the spectrum and its full "
"covariance matrix"
msgstr "**Bootstrap PSD 推定**はスペクトルとその完全な共分散行列の両方を提供する"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470007
#: eab64f1e0373426ca4d6de84953bee29
msgid ""
"**Overlapping segments** introduce correlations that standard methods ignore"
msgstr "**オーバーラップするセグメント**は標準的な手法では無視される相関を導入する"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470008
#: 65dc959959d34fc09b10e86a98291b14
msgid ""
"**GLS fitting** properly weights data according to the covariance structure"
msgstr "**GLS フィッティング**は共分散構造に基づいてデータを適切に重み付けする"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470009
#: b7977833df0e4d7fa127e4023728a894
msgid "**MCMC** provides robust posterior distributions for complex models"
msgstr "**MCMC** は複雑なモデルに対してロバストな事後分布を提供する"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470010
#: e9449e10a5744248b5b84a5653eeab5d
msgid "**OLS underestimates errors** when correlations are present"
msgstr "**OLS は相関が存在する場合に誤差を過小評価**する"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470012
#: b40e060be50042e78b88a38eb1e6d391
msgid "Recommended Workflow"
msgstr "推奨ワークフロー"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470030
#: b436cb59ccd849dfab89a3dc4e7794a4
msgid "Common Pitfalls"
msgstr "よくある落とし穴"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470032
#: 8de13548a2db4cbda6d852728b2549ec
msgid "**Using OLS for correlated data** → underestimated errors"
msgstr "**相関のあるデータに OLS を使用**する → 誤差の過小評価"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470033
#: 83002b92b9164ed6b185ffaa44b444dd
msgid "**Too few bootstrap samples** → noisy covariance estimate"
msgstr "**Bootstrap サンプル数が少なすぎる** → 共分散推定にノイズが混入"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470034
#: d280df91b1e54d189b0ae1d388130d25
msgid "**Poor initial guesses** → fit may converge to local minimum"
msgstr "**初期推定値が不適切** → 局所最小値に収束する可能性"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bootstrap_gls_fitting.ipynb:470035
#: 12454413aded4287a7fe2139b413bf03
msgid "**Forgetting to crop covariance** → dimension mismatch errors"
msgstr "**共分散のクロップを忘れる** → 次元の不一致エラー"

